    {
      "id": "O-003",
      "title": "setA-13 is stochastically feasible",
      "description": "setA-13 (2000 demands, 1000 links) was infeasible in campaign v1 but feasible in campaigns v2 and v3. This demonstrates that the feasible region exists but is difficult to reach under random initialization. Confirmed stochastically feasible."
    },
    {
      "id": "O-004",
      "title": "Evaluation cost scales with demands x links",
      "description": "ms/gen increases from 131ms (setA-01: 40d x 80l) to 102873ms (setA-13: 2000d x 1000l), a ~785x increase. This quantifies the O(demands x links) evaluation bottleneck targeted by RP-310 (incremental evaluation)."
    },
    {
      "id": "O-005",
      "title": "Network topology materially affects feasibility",
      "description": "setA-13 (2000d, 1000l, ratio=0.50) is stochastically feasible while setA-16 (4800d, 1452l) is robustly infeasible. setA-17 (2000d, 1270l, ratio=0.64) is consistently feasible. Demand count alone does not determine feasibility."
    }
